.TH POWEROFF 1 "" "" "mcos Manual"
.SH NAME
poweroff \- turn the computer off
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B poweroff
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B poweroff
ends every process, closing their files (so what they wrote reaches the
disks), and turns the computer off, as its power button does. It takes
no arguments.
.SH EXIT STATUS
It does not return when it works. If the kernel refuses, the reason is
printed and the status is 1.
.SH NOTES
What a process had buffered in its own standard I/O and not yet written
is lost, as on Linux; programs should close their files first.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR reboot (1),
.BR halt (1)
